          name: "Where can I get Gold’s Gym treadmill parts?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Start with the GGTL model number on the frame sticker. iFIT, which was ICON, is the manufacturer’s route for parts, and specialist suppliers such as FitnessRepairParts.com list Gold’s Gym treadmills by model number. Third-party walking belts, drive belts and safety keys for the 430i and 720 are sold on Amazon and Walmart; check their listed model numbers against yours.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a Gold’s Gym treadmill good?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They were budget treadmills, and reviewers were mixed: one long-running site was not overly impressed with the line, another found the Trainer 720 acceptable for its price. Used, a working one can be a reasonable walking machine if it is cheap. For a new purchase, the same maker’s current ProForm and NordicTrack folders are the like-for-like choice.",
